\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 Social Post Style Ideas:\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs26 \cf0 \
You can absolutely build a tight visual system around those four: calm, stoic, protective, local.\
\pard\pardeftab560\sa40\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32 \cf0 Core vibe translation\
\pard\pardeftab560\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\f2\b0\fs18 \cf0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f0\b\fs26 Calm
\f1\b0 : Soft, desaturated colors (muted blue/teal/green), generous whitespace, minimal clutter.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f2\fs18 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f0\b\fs26 Stoic
\f1\b0 : Simple geometry, clean type, minimal decoration, consistent grid; no loud gradients or gimmicky effects.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f2\fs18 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f0\b\fs26 Protective
\f1\b0 : Clear hierarchy, strong shapes (shields, circles, \'93home\'94 outlines), solid blocks behind key text to feel reliable.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f2\fs18 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f0\b\fs26 Local
\f1\b0 : Subtle neighborhood cues\'97street maps, house silhouettes, city blocks, small photo details from real neighborhoods.\
\pard\pardeftab560\sa40\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32 \cf0 Palette and type direction\
\pard\pardeftab560\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0
\f2\b0\fs18 \cf0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f1\fs26 Colors\
\pard\pardeftab560\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl1
\f2\fs18 \cf0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f1\fs26 Primary: a muted deep blue or blue-green (trust + calm).\
\ls2\ilvl1
\f2\fs18 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f1\fs26 Secondary: a soft warm accent (muted orange or yellow) used sparingly for CTAs and alerts.\
\ls2\ilvl1
\f2\fs18 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f1\fs26 Support: light neutral background (off-white/very light gray) plus a dark charcoal for text.\
\pard\pardeftab560\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0
\f2\fs18 \cf0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f1\fs26 Typography\
\pard\pardeftab560\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl1
\f2\fs18 \cf0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f1\fs26 Headings: a modern, slightly condensed sans (stoic, serious but not corporate-stiff).\
\ls2\ilvl1
\f2\fs18 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f1\fs26 Body: a friendly, open sans-serif with good legibility at small sizes.\
\ls2\ilvl1
\f2\fs18 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f1\fs26 Style: mostly sentence case, low exclamation-point usage, short, declarative sentences (\'93Know your nearby allies.\'94).\
\pard\pardeftab560\sa40\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32 \cf0 Layout patterns for posts\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs26 \cf0 For each Safe Neighbor post type, keep these structural rules:\
\pard\pardeftab560\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0
\f2\fs18 \cf0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f1\fs26 \'93Tip\'94 posts\
\pard\pardeftab560\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl1
\f2\fs18 \cf0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f1\fs26 Top bar: small label pill (e.g., \'93Safety Tip\'94).\
\ls3\ilvl1
\f2\fs18 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f1\fs26 Big calm headline, plenty of breathing room.\
\ls3\ilvl1
\f2\fs18 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f1\fs26 3\'964 short lines of body text, no walls of text.\
\ls3\ilvl1
\f2\fs18 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f1\fs26 Small icon in a circle (door, key, phone) in one corner.\
\pard\pardeftab560\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0
\f2\fs18 \cf0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f1\fs26 \'93Protective alert explainer\'94\
\pard\pardeftab560\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl1
\f2\fs18 \cf0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f1\fs26 Strong top band in primary color with white text: \'93How Safe Neighbor Helps\'94.\
\ls3\ilvl1
\f2\fs18 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f1\fs26 Center block: 1\'962 short bullets explaining the protection.\
\ls3\ilvl1
\f2\fs18 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f1\fs26 Accent badge for the CTA (e.g., \'93Add trusted neighbor\'94).\
\ls3\ilvl1
\f2\fs18 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f1\fs26 Keep colors steady so alerts don\'92t feel panicky, just clear.\
\pard\pardeftab560\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0
\f2\fs18 \cf0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f1\fs26 \'93Local story/neighbor highlight\'94\
\pard\pardeftab560\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl1
\f2\fs18 \cf0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f1\fs26 Photo (or illustration) of a house/block/neighborhood with a soft overlay.\
\ls3\ilvl1
\f2\fs18 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f1\fs26 Text panel that feels like a calm notice board: \'93A neighbor\'92s story\'94, quote, name or pseudonym, area (e.g., \'93Clintonville\'94).\
\ls3\ilvl1
\f2\fs18 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f1\fs26 Small map-pin or street icon.\
\pard\pardeftab560\sa40\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32 \cf0 How this ties into your tools\
\pard\pardeftab560\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0
\f2\b0\fs18 \cf0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f1\fs26 Design the system once (in Figma or Kittl): define the palette, type choices, and those three\'96four layout patterns with locked structure.\
\ls4\ilvl0
\f2\fs18 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f1\fs26 For automation later (using Sheets), treat each post as:\
\pard\pardeftab560\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl1
\f2\fs18 \cf0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f1\fs26 Fixed \'93frame\'94 + slots: label, headline, body, cta, neighborhood_name, image.\
\ls4\ilvl1
\f2\fs18 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f1\fs26 This keeps every generated post feeling calm, stoic, protective, and local because only the text/image changes, not the overall composition.\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0
